@@ -12,3 +12,8 @@ after its title changes. `get(id)` returns the task with that id, and `find`, `c
 `rename`, `tag`, `untag` and `remove` take either a title or an id (a title wins over an id written the
 same). Ids are `task-1`, `task-2`, … in the order tasks are added, and are never reused; they are counted
 rather than random so the domain stays deterministic.
+
+Every task has `createdAt` and `updatedAt`, ISO-8601 date-times. They are the same when the task is added;
+every change (complete, reopen, rename, tag, untag) sets `updatedAt` to the time of the change, and a
+refused change leaves it alone. The domain never reads the clock: `createTodoList(now?)` takes a function
+that tells the time, the system clock by default, so tests can pass a fixed one.
